If I were to host a special dinner and choose guests from history to converse with, I would invite:

1. Leonardo da Vinci - for discussions on art, science, and philosophy;
2. Albert Einstein - to explore the mysteries of our universe;
3. Isaac Newton - to talk about physics and mathematics;
4. Ada Lovelace - to discuss the early days of computing and artificial intelligence;
5. Nikola Tesla - to explore the possibilities of electricity and energy.

These conversations would be fascinating and enlightening, covering a wide range of topics and eras in human history.
